Subject: [PATCH 1/5] =?UTF-8?q?=F0=9F=94=A5=20fix(generate)!:=20drop=20the?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20sampling-temperature=20rung?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

interactiveTemperature was injected through CLAUDE_CODE_EXTRA_BODY as the
first rung of the attempt ladder. Claude Code runs the model with thinking
on, and the API then rejects every temperature except the default:

  API Error: 400 `temperature` may only be set to 1 when thinking is
  enabled or in adaptive mode

(verified live against claude-sonnet-5, which the default `sonnet` alias
serves). So the shipped default (1) was byte-for-byte the API default - a
no-op - and any other value cost a failed round trip (~1.5 s) before the
ladder silently retried without it. The 0..2 clamp also admitted values
above the Messages API's 0..1 range.

Variety between interactive candidates already comes from the prompt:
buildUser asks for 'exactly N distinct command options - genuinely
different approaches or tools', all returned by one structured call.

- remove Config.interactiveTemperature, its default and sanitising
- remove RunPromptOptions/SubprocessEnvOptions.temperature and the
  CLAUDE_CODE_EXTRA_BODY merge in buildSubprocessEnv
- the ladder is now structured -> plain text
- tests: drop the temperature cases, pin that a user's own
  CLAUDE_CODE_EXTRA_BODY passes through untouched, and that several
  candidates come from one call
- README, design spec (pipeline, config, testing, decisions log)

BREAKING CHANGE: the interactiveTemperature config key is ignored (unknown
keys already are), so existing config files keep loading.
